{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>In the firmament of the heavens, to illuminate upon the earth.</b> For so is the way to suspend a lamp in a high place. According to its plain sense, the sun and moon were needed to illuminate upon the earth. And the light created on the first day was to illuminate the heavens, because the firmament that was created on the second day became a barrier between the primordial light and the earth. Alternatively, what is written ויהי אור — that is the light of day, and here it is the light of the sun and the moon. Even though there were not yet creatures that would need illumination, nevertheless there were already grasses and fruits, which need to be ripened by the sun and the moon, as it says: וממגד תבואות שמש. And further, because the creeping creatures, living souls, and birds that were created on the fifth day needed it, therefore he prepared light for them beforehand."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:19:22.097003845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}